#OBSERVATIONALSTUDY

BLURB
Design and interpret observational studies.

PITCH
“A few observations and much reasoning lead to error; many observations and a little reasoning to truth.” - Alexis Carrel

PARAGRAPH DESCRIPTION
Science typically begins with observation. Only after phenomena have been described can one search for patterns and principles that underlie them. The nature of observational studies varies in different disciplines, but in all cases the researcher measures variables without manipulating them. It is critical that observational studies are designed to ensure that measurements are careful, systematic, and unbiased. Different observational study designs each have strengths and weaknesses, but can effectively test hypotheses.

